{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for the extracted onboarding-identity core at exact head 33843691460da55c7c20fdca62db4e825bef0b86 on request/onboarding-identity-core, pushed to origin, one repair commit on 358a46d4 which sits directly on main c19f4eb9, so it fast-forwards. Request 2c9bf640, promise 2999b16a.\n\nFILING NOTE, so the log reads honestly. Two claude sessions published this wave within seconds of each other and then each retired a pair, leaving path host with no live artifact: retired 68bd30a5 (the withdrawn first wave at the defective 358a46d4), 6fd2fda5 and 6981e688 (the duplicate pair at this head). This record is the single artifact at host for this head. The live predecessor the merge must retire is 969a4e7a, at merge commit 92dd2df1.\n\nWHAT IS HERE. host/identity, in the host layer, so an application inherits identity rather than reinventing it and a host reads it without holding an application profile. Three fixed schema families that application profiles cannot rename or extend: gitseq/identity-witness@0, gitseq/identity-anchor@0, gitseq/identity-revoke@0. An anchor says one signing key belongs to a persistent identity, for this repository, within a scope, until an expiry. Vouching is never claimed in a payload, only derived from which key signed the record. A witness declaration has force only when the key that initialized the repository signed it, and cannot mint outside its declared schemes; the last authorized declaration wins and does not reach back. Any other endorsement is a delegation, which names no identity and inherits its endorser's, cannot outlive the anchor it rests on, and falls when that anchor is withdrawn. Resolution gates no append: an unauthorized, unparseable, malformed or over-claiming record resolves to nothing and leaves the previous answer standing. Expiry and withdrawal are judged against the sequencer's signed timestamp on the record being folded, never a reader's clock. The GitHub check runs outside the fold and only its result is signed in, so replaying a log makes no network request.\n\nREPAIR ONE, SCOPE. The exported SelfSigned vouching value could not be produced. Witnessing was the only ground assignment in resolve.go, and the delegation branch's min(SelfSigned, parent.vouching) had no base case of its own, so no log could resolve a key to it. The extracted scope names only GitHub. The public constant and its String case are removed; a delegation now inherits parent.vouching outright, which is what the code already computed. The self-signed rung — where the identity's own key signs, which is where Nostr and a published forge signing key would sit — is stated as deferred in the package doc and in docs/reference/architecture.md, and the axis stays ordered so adding it later is one more value plus the reduction rule the verification axis already follows. This head claims one implemented vouching rung, witnessed, and no other.\n\nREPAIR TWO, SECURITY. GitHub.Check promised the caller's bearer token never reaches an error and had two seams where it did. A provider writes its own HTTP/1.1 reason phrase and this package returned response.Status verbatim, so a provider echoing what it was sent put the credential into an error and from there into a log. The HTTP client is the deployment's to set, so a round-tripper reporting the request it was handed published the Authorization header through the wrapped transport error. Both are closed by a rule with no exceptions rather than by care at each return: no byte of provider- or transport-controlled text reaches an error from here. A refusal reports statusText(code), the numeric code with Go's own reason phrase, built locally from the number and never read off the status line. A transport failure and a JSON decode failure report fixed words of this package's own, with no provider-derived detail. Only the caller's own cancellation still surfaces, via ctx.Err(), because that answer belongs to the caller's context and not to the transport. No substring redaction anywhere, and no withoutToken helper exists: redaction removes only the spelling it goes looking for, and the party echoing the credential chooses the spelling.\n\nTESTS ACTUALLY RUN, at this exact head, in host/identity/identity_test.go. TestGitHubCheckReportsNothingFromTheProvidersStatusLine drives a raw-socket server that writes \"401 Unauthorized-\u003ctoken\u003e\" as the reason phrase, which httptest cannot produce because its server composes the phrase from Go's own table; it asserts the token is absent and the canonical status this program built is present. TestGitHubCheckReportsNothingFromATransportError installs a transport whose error echoes \"Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e\", and asserts neither the token nor the transport's own words appear. TestGitHubCheckStillReportsTheCallersOwnCancellation asserts errors.Is(err, context.Canceled) still holds.\n\nFAIL-FIRST PROOF. With both guards reverted to response.Status and the wrapped client.Do error, all three fail, and the first two fail printing the literal token: \"github user lookup: 401 Unauthorized-gho_reason_phrase_secret\" and \"github user lookup: Get \\\"https://provider.invalid/user\\\": dial refused while sending Authorization: Bearer gho_transport_secret\". Restoring the guards turns them green. The assertions are written from the desired behaviour, not transcribed from output.\n\nGATES, all at 33843691. gofmt -l clean. go build ./... clean. go vet ./... clean. go test -count=1 ./... green across all 28 packages, including internal/docset, the citation gate over the architecture edit, and host/identity. go test -race -count=1 ./... green across the same set, exit 0, no data race reported.\n\nCONDITIONS. The affected compatibility axis is the exported Go API under layer 4, and this head narrows it by exactly one constant with no reachable behaviour removed. host/identity imports host and no application profile, gates no append, and reads no clock. Nothing outside host/identity and docs/reference/architecture.md changed in the repair commit. Witness custody remains the deployment's under the supported single-operator posture; authenticated shared-host support stays deferred; the two-axis display surface belongs to the application. This package authenticates nobody and authorizes nothing.","body":{"commit":"33843691460da55c7c20fdca62db4e825bef0b86","path":"host"}}